{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b> אני ה'.</b> Even though I said 'and you shall be to him for Elohim,' I did not say it in the sense of fear — for I am HaShem, that is to say: I alone am the one to be feared. Rashi explained: faithful to pay a good reward, etc.; 'אני ה'‎' — faithful to exact payment. And if you ask: how does this imply that this name specifically suggests 'faithful to pay a good reward and faithful to exact payment' more than the other names of HaShem? Rather, since this name is written in the tetragrammaton form, as he explained in the section of Shemot, it conveys that He is and exists forever without end, and in His hand to repay every creature its due whenever He wishes."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:23.373520895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}